<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Admin | Fragments | {{siteName}}</title>
    {{>partials/head-deps.hbs}}
    {{>partials/head-styles.hbs}}
</head>
<body>
{{>partials/admin-shell.hbs}}
    <div class="page-meta"><h1><i class="mdi mdi-puzzle-outline" aria-hidden="true"></i> Fragments</h1><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/a/fragments/new">New fragment</a></div>
    {{#otherSite}}<div class="alert alert-warning" role="alert"><i class="mdi mdi-information-outline" aria-hidden="true"></i> That fragment belongs to a different site. Showing <strong>{{managedSiteName}}</strong>'s fragments instead.</div>{{/otherSite}}
    <p class="text-secondary">Reusable content included in pages with <code>&#123;&#123;fragment:key&#125;&#125;</code>. Resolved for the page's locale, falling back to the default locale.</p>
    {{! data-sort-type marks a column click-to-sort (see WkBrowserCore.enableTableSort); the Edit column
        deliberately carries none. "Used by" sorts on the raw count, not its "N page(s)" text. }}
    {{! table-responsive: enableColumnResize switches the table to a fixed layout that can end up wider
        than the admin content column, so the overflow has to scroll here rather than in the page body. }}
    <div class="table-responsive">
    <table class="table table-hover align-middle" id="fragmentsTable">
        <thead><tr>
            <th data-sort-type="text">Key</th>
            <th data-sort-type="text">Locale</th>
            <th data-sort-type="text">Title</th>
            <th data-sort-type="number">Used by</th>
            <th></th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{#fragments}}
        <tr>
            {{! data-sort pins the sort to the key alone — the copy button contributes no text today,
                but the cell's own value is the honest thing to sort on. copy-inline.js (site-wide)
                handles the click. }}
            <td data-sort="{{key}}">{{key}}<button type="button" class="copy-inline-btn" data-copy="{{key}}" title="Copy key" aria-label="Copy key {{key}} to clipboard"><i class="mdi mdi-content-copy" aria-hidden="true"></i></button></td>
            <td>{{locale}}</td>
            <td>{{title}}</td>
            <td data-sort="{{usedBy}}">{{usedBy}} page(s)</td>
            <td><a class="btn btn-sm btn-primary" href="/a/fragments/{{id}}/edit">Edit</a></td>
        </tr>
        {{/fragments}}
        </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    {{! The inverse of the "Used by" column: pages asking for a fragment that isn't there, which render
        a visible "[missing fragment: key]" marker for readers. Grouped by key -- one row is one
        fragment to create (or one rename to undo). }}
    {{#hasMissing}}
    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Missing fragments <span class="badge text-bg-secondary">{{missingCount}}</span></h2>
    <p class="text-secondary">
        These keys are referenced but no fragment provides them, so every place below renders
        <code>[missing fragment: key]</code> instead of content. A fragment may have been deleted or
        renamed, or the reference may just be a typo.
    </p>
    <div class="table-responsive">
    <table class="table table-hover align-middle">
        <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>References</th><th>Referenced from</th><th></th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{#missing}}
        <tr>
            <td><code>{{key}}</code></td>
            <td>{{refCount}}</td>
            <td>
                <ul class="list-unstyled mb-0">
                {{#sources}}
                    <li><span class="badge text-bg-light">{{type}}</span> <a href="{{url}}">{{label}}</a> <span class="text-secondary">({{locale}})</span></li>
                {{/sources}}
                </ul>
            </td>
            {{! The query string is literal here on purpose: Mustache escapes "=" in an interpolated
                value, so building the whole URL server-side would emit "?key&#61;…". }}
            <td class="text-end"><a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" href="/a/fragments/new?key={{key}}">Create</a></td>
        </tr>
        {{/missing}}
        </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    {{/hasMissing}}

    {{! Click-to-sort, plus drag-to-resize on desktop (enableColumnResize no-ops on touch/narrow screens). }}
    <script src="/static/wk-browser.js?v={{assetVersion}}"></script>
    <script>
      (function () {
        var table = document.getElementById('fragmentsTable');
        if (!table || !window.WkBrowserCore) return;
        window.WkBrowserCore.ensureStyle();
        window.WkBrowserCore.enableTableSort(table, 'fragments');
        window.WkBrowserCore.enableColumnResize(table, 'fragments');
      })();
    </script>
{{>partials/admin-shell-end.hbs}}
{{{bodyHtml}}}</body>
</html>
